        "original_id": "7f473f5d-af30-5b75-8fb7-427000967446",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: The Venetian Macao, The Venetian Las Vegas, Macau\n- Events: 10th IIFA Awards\n- Companies: KlingStubbins\n- Topics: building size, design, hotel towers\n\nFacts:\n- The Venetian Macao has 10,500,000 square feet of floor area and is the seventh-largest building in the world by floor area.\n- The Venetian Macao is modeled on its sister casino resort, The Venetian Las Vegas.\n- From June 11 to June 13, 2009, the 10th IIFA Awards ceremony was held at The Venetian Macao in Macau.\n- KlingStubbins designed the hotel tower of The Venetian Las Vegas.\n- The hotel tower of The Venetian Las Vegas contains 36 stories and rises 475 feet.",
